#: f51e7bcc5ec4448ba55d214a575f0c9e
msgid ""
"This document records the durable contract for Jittor's native complex "
"dtype. Implementation history and individual experiment transcripts "
"belong in Git and `agent/results/`; they are intentionally not duplicated"
" here."
msgstr ""

#: 2ebef366b4fb440780b9e024b001b547
msgid "Decision"
msgstr ""

#: cbb07461ac2c45669b4004e2005f6492
msgid ""
"`complex64` is a first-class `jittor_core` dtype. Public tensor APIs "
"should consume and return native complex `Var` objects. The older "
"`jt.nn.ComplexNumber` real/imaginary pair remains only as an internal "
"bridge for linear-algebra algorithms that have not yet been rewritten. "
"New public APIs must not introduce another simulated complex "
"representation."
msgstr ""

#: bbb3964a3c7c4471946f14bf392bd5bd
msgid ""
"`complex128` is not registered. Adding it requires expanding and auditing"
" the core dtype-size representation before exposing any constructor or "
"promotion rule."
msgstr ""

#: 684edd1ff7864a689415cae678b6473d
msgid "Supported contract"
msgstr ""

#: 638dd1c9717a42059016bbdf7d80c475
msgid "The maintained CPU and CUDA tests cover:"
msgstr ""

#: 496ce3eb3a68467fb86a66cb2484df24
msgid ""
"construction from NumPy complex64, zero initialization, scalar "
"assignment, NumPy round trips, and real/complex casts;"
msgstr ""

#: 07ebb6eefcc34a798e47efecdb23ec67
msgid ""
"add, subtract, multiply, divide, negate, scalar mixing, equality, "
"inequality, and ternary selection;"
msgstr ""

#: c850f7ce58f7468a90be819cc6a7c6a2
msgid ""
"reshape, transpose, indexing, slicing, broadcasting, concatenation, and "
"stack;"
msgstr ""

#: fa9072cee9184f3d8133849ae68a4f18
msgid "`sum`, `mean`, `abs`, `conj`, 2-D and batched matrix multiplication;"
msgstr ""

#: 6631e088c6a34138a881203a651f4a0b
msgid "`exp`, `log`, `sin`, `cos`, and `sqrt`;"
msgstr ""

#: 9d699b14275d41a88687e1d13b2a5274
msgid ""
"`.real`, `.imag`, `.angle()`, `view_as_real`, `view_as_complex`, and "
"`polar`;"
msgstr ""

#: 610ed8f4f60b47e48f40336ed9146c52
msgid ""
"Wirtinger-style first-order gradients for supported arithmetic, "
"magnitude, matrix multiplication, bridge operations, and transcendental "
"functions;"
msgstr ""

#: 79e5130845d744e18a01912c74fd4e17
msgid ""
"native-complex inputs and outputs for FFT, VJP, and the maintained "
"linear-algebra surface."
msgstr ""

