msgstr ""

#: 84f937f8ce394ac585520fb0d0d169be
msgid "Dtype and gradient invariants"
msgstr ""

#: 47e436a556e943b2829ef0441f3039c6
msgid ""
"`complex64` has an eight-byte element size and is classified as complex, "
"not floating-point or integer."
msgstr ""

#: dc7d4905c036486a80cfbc17f64e5de3
msgid ""
"Complex-to-real casts select the real component. Complex-to-bool is true "
"when either component is nonzero."
msgstr ""

#: e100febcd315463da7475678a72e774b
msgid ""
"`abs(complex64)` returns `float32`; arithmetic and complex reductions "
"retain `complex64` unless an explicit contract says otherwise."
msgstr ""

#: be35cf6a19814431ae24a3262e226223
msgid ""
"A differentiable complex value is allowed to carry gradients, but a "
"scalar loss supplied to reverse-mode differentiation remains real."
msgstr ""

#: 15ab92898c4d464ba2d52e881abf1193
msgid ""
"Complex binary gradients conjugate the opposite operand according to the "
"real-loss convention used by Torch. Holomorphic unary gradients conjugate"
" the local derivative."
msgstr ""

#: 70ff7efb52f84f9295c1bdb1e3003879
msgid "Unsupported gradients fail explicitly; they do not silently return zeros."
msgstr ""

#: 35dd75a312e9462b8dea3e2db8481020
msgid "Bridge boundary"
msgstr ""

#: e0577da977d544989377eeb2c8ca6a49
msgid ""
"`view_as_real` and its inverse convert between `complex64[...]` and "
"`float32[..., 2]` on device and preserve first-order gradients. The "
"conversion is an implementation bridge, not a promise of zero-copy "
"aliasing."
msgstr ""

#: 41c29ed8e04b411d8d662b2ca3dba125
msgid ""
"Some functions in `jittor.linalg` currently convert native values to the "
"internal `ComplexNumber` substrate, execute an existing real/imaginary "
"algorithm, and convert outputs back to native complex tensors. That "
"substrate is deprecated for user-facing results but cannot be deleted "
"until all such kernels have native implementations and equivalent tests."
msgstr ""

#: 7a78c70569fb434e898d5f923a3f7152
msgid "Known limitations"
msgstr ""

#: 8de421c40f714392a8de4fb1855c9c3d
msgid ""
"CUDA complex `prod` lacks the required atomic multiply implementation. "
"CPU is covered; CUDA must fail rather than return a partial result."
msgstr ""

#: a8d6f718980547ffae805f4d6e8f9290
msgid ""
"Native complex JVP relies on second-order autograd that is not "
"implemented. `jvp` raises `NotImplementedError`; native complex VJP is "
"supported."
msgstr ""

#: e3d0814b5ecc4478a4021bc7a0ab6c1b
msgid ""
"General complex eigendecomposition on CUDA depends on an available CuPy "
"linear-algebra path and may be unavailable in otherwise valid CUDA "
"setups."
msgstr ""

#: 8154f60fec8748dd8a400a6984e3716a
msgid "`complex128` and several transcendental operations are unsupported."
msgstr ""

#: b3d594735dab4a19ad570178d3d32d48
msgid ""
"Native complex linear algebra still uses the internal bridge described "
"above."
msgstr ""

#: 9d1f080464074829a641d2d7f1c021b1
msgid ""
"These limitations are indexed in the [known-issues "
"ledger](https://github.com/Jittor/jittor/blob/master/agent/manuals/known-"
"issues.md). A limitation is removed only together with a focused "
"regression that exercises the previously unsupported backend or "
"derivative order."
msgstr ""

#: 7d01aaec31c04e42b8309ca3b8361885
msgid "Extension checklist"
msgstr ""

#: 55305785fb4b423ab7b5abc0e3cfaa01
msgid "When adding a complex operation:"
msgstr ""

#: 06cf9211a43949748fc01e55cbd1484b
msgid "Specify input promotion and output dtype independently from kernel code."
msgstr ""

#: 4876817423ef4b758ec356be101a6fcf
msgid "Add CPU forward comparison against NumPy or a precise mathematical oracle."
msgstr ""

#: 22864f5122b243bd980d74bdc63e595b
msgid ""
"Add CUDA/NPU execution and device-parity coverage where support is "
"claimed."
msgstr ""

#: baec90998f49449184e380c7d63c25bb
msgid "Derive and test first-order gradients under the real-loss convention."
msgstr ""

#: b42388539da146998522ca935ef0c226
msgid ""
"Test zero, branch-cut, empty, batched, and non-contiguous cases as "
"applicable."
msgstr ""

#: 77c7e475e0d64ac2822281960fd9a068
msgid "Raise an explicit error for unsupported derivative orders or backends."
msgstr ""

